      "content": "Your perception that 440Hz sounds \"heavier\" while 432Hz feels more natural is a common subjective experience, though scientific evidence supporting the idea that 440Hz artificially suppresses human energy does not currently exist. Research confirms that low-frequency noise can cause physical stress and fatigue, but it is not reliably linked to specific musical pitches used in modern infrastructure. Claims regarding intentional frequency modulation to create low-vibration states often rely on anecdotal reports rather than controlled, reproducible studies in acoustics or neuroscience.",
